{"id": "section-body-12574", "title": "Genital Warts (Venereal Warts)", "chapterId": "chapter-twelve", "tocLevel": 4, "tocPath": ["APPROACH TO PATIENTS WITH EMERGENCY CONDITIONS", "SEXUALLY TRANSMITTED INFECTIONS", "Late Syphilis", "Genital Warts (Venereal Warts)"], "blocks": [{"id": "body-12574", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Genital Warts (Venereal Warts)", "runs": [{"text": "Genital"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Warts"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(Venereal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Warts)"}], "level": 4, "list": {"level": 2, "numberingId": "1397"}}, {"id": "body-12575", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Human papilloma virus (HPV) is a common sexually transmitted pathogen. Genital warts are painless but may lead to serious complications. The removal of the lesion does not mean cure of the infection. No treatment is completely satisfactory. Recommended regimens for venereal warts are as follows:", "runs": [{"text": "Human papilloma virus (HPV)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is a common sexually transmitted pathogen."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Genital"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "warts are painless but"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "may lead to serious complications. The removal of the lesion does not mean cure of the infection. No treatment is completely satisfactory. Recommended regimens for venereal warts are as follows:"}]}, {"id": "body-12577", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Pharmacological Management", "runs": [{"text": "Pharmacological"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Management"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-12578", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "D: podophyllin 10–25% in compound tincture of benzoin, applied carefully to the warts, avoiding normal tissue. External genital and perianal warts should be washed thoroughly 4–6 hourly after the application of podophyllin.", "runs": [{"text": "D:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "podophyllin"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "10–25%"}, {"t